<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mildburh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 715</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Milburga, Saint Milburga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mildburh was a daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merewalh">Merewalh</a> of the Magonsaete and the first abbess of the double monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/much-wenlock">Wenlock</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shropshire">Shropshire</a>, founded around 680. Venerated as a saint, she was credited with miracles, and the rediscovery of her relics by the Cluniac monks of Wenlock in 1101 revived her cult.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mildburh.jpg" alt="Mildburh" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan de las Roelas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santa_Milburga_-_Juan_de_Roelas_20140706.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
